{
  "title": "About Rcntable Plugin",
  "story": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2c688709b8866b4d",
      "text": "The Rcntable plugin puts a table of records on a wiki page. The page shows the shape of the table - how many rows by how many columns, the column names as chips, the first few names as links - and an Open Table button that opens the whole table in a popup: scan, sort, filter, select rows, compare them, then follow one row into a drawing of what it is connected to, or put the selected rows on a map."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5628a97a8e10fbf1",
      "text": "Create an item with the factory and press Open Table. In the popup, choose the records and the kind of thing, then use -> Wiki item to write what you are looking at back onto the page. Every name is a link: click one and that subject opens beside the table. Hover a column chip and any chart on the same page responds to it."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "56dfcc7b574ef904",
      "text": "Where the records come from: the popup reads a folder in this site's assets, /assets/rcn-table/, holding one exported database per subfolder. The folder is written by substrate/export.py from the site owner's own files. So each site is its own database - whoever owns the site is its keeper, and anyone who can read the page can read the table. Nothing here talks to a database server. An item may carry src to read another site's folder instead."
    },
    {
      "type": "rcntable",
      "id": "d0dbe915091d400b",
      "text": "",
      "database": "whatcom",
      "kind": "Entity"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "54c5088e8dc74b7a",
      "text": "Developed by Marc Pierson with Claude Opus 5 (Anthropic) for the ReLocalize Creativity Network. Source: [[RCN Table]] - tools/rcn-table.html, tools/rcn-table-map.html and wiki-plugin-rcn-table in the rcn repository."
    }
  ],
